{%- comment -%}
  Renders a thin line SVG icon for the Shudhi homepage sections.

  Usage: {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}
         {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right', class: 'my-class' %}

  Available: shudhi-mark, leaf, drop, heart, hand, rabbit, lotus, wind, eye,
  sparkle, mortar, plant, bottle, recycle, badge, shield, search, user, cart,
  menu, close, arrow-right, arrow-up, chevron-left, chevron-right, play,
  instagram, facebook, pinterest, youtube
  Fine-line trust-bar set: leaf-line, heart-line, hand-line, rabbit-line, flask-line
  Our Story set: wheat, sprout, flower, sun, hands-heart, heart-check
  Bath-ritual set: meditate, body, face-sparkle, shower, bubbles
  Contact set: pin, phone, mail, clock, alert
  Product-page set: plus, minus, lock, truck, file
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign n = name | default: 'leaf' -%}
{%- comment -%} Optional `sw` overrides stroke weight, for the finer line art
    used in the nav and the hero trust bar. Defaults to the library weight. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign stroke_w = sw | default: 1.4 -%}
{%- capture cls -%}sh-icon sh-icon--{{ n }}{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}{%- endcapture -%}
<svg class="{{ cls }}" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="{{ stroke_w }}" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
{%- comment -%}
  `draw` — opt-in, and OFF for every caller that does not ask. Captures the glyph
  and stamps pathLength="1" onto each of its shapes, which normalises every path
  to one unit of length so a caller can draw it on with
  `stroke-dasharray: 1; stroke-dashoffset: 1 -> 0` and no JS measurement at all.
  See shudhi-story.css §28's [data-sh-draw] primitive; sections/sh-story-philosophy.liquid
  is the only caller today.

  WHY THIS IS SAFE ACROSS ALL ~54 CALL SITES

  1. `draw` is nil everywhere else, so the replace never runs and the captured
     string is emitted exactly as the case block produced it — byte-identical
     output, verified by diffing the rendered homepage before and after.
  2. The three match strings each end in a SPACE, and the file contains only
     `<path ` (99), `<circle ` (26) and `<rect ` (3) — no <line>, <polyline> or
     <ellipse> exist here. Nothing else in the string can match.
  3. Even a leaked `draw: true` is INERT. pathLength has no rendering effect
     whatsoever unless a stroke-dasharray is in play, and the only dasharray rules
     in the theme are scoped to .sh-ritual__connectors, .sh-mindful, .sh-lc__arc
     and .sh-ritual__trace — none of which can reach an .sh-icon child.
  4. The case block below is untouched. No bezier is ever hand-edited, so the
     glyph library cannot drift from the drawable version of itself.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture glyph -%}
